 r"I am writing to apply for the AI Delivery Specialist position at CPM UK. I completed an MSc in Health Data Science at University College London in September 2026, where a distinction is expected, after a BSc in Biological Sciences at Imperial College London, and I currently work as a Data Analyst Intern at TikTok Shop UK.",

 r"This role appeals to me because it covers the whole journey of an AI solution: understanding what a team actually needs, building the agent or automation, testing it with users, and helping people adopt it. Some of my most satisfying work so far has followed a similar path.",

 r"At TikTok Shop UK I noticed that one of our analytics tasks followed the same logic each time, so I used Claude Code to build an AI agent that automates its repetitive steps, with a validation step to check the outputs. It is now used by my own team and by adjacent teams. Getting there meant understanding the existing process before deciding what to automate. Day to day I also build KPI frameworks and dashboards and present recommendations to operations, product and commercial stakeholders.",

 r"At DS Digital Technology I worked with a pharmaceutical client on a patient-facing AI assistant. I turned the client's requirements into a 246-question benchmark and a six-dimension rubric with red-line rules for unsafe answers, which the client adopted as its acceptance standard. I built a Python pipeline that tested six LLMs with retrieval and search augmentation and scored more than 2,400 responses, ran blinded A/B tests of a medically reviewed knowledge graph, and presented the results and risks to the client's stakeholders. This gave me a practical grounding in responsible AI: deciding what a system must never do, testing for it, and explaining the limitations clearly.",

 r"I should be clear about one gap. I use Excel and Power BI regularly, but I have not yet built agents in Microsoft Copilot Studio or Power Automate; my agent and automation work so far has used Python, LLM APIs and Claude Code. I learn new platforms quickly and would expect to be productive with Copilot tooling early on.",

 r"I have the right to work in the UK until January 2029, after which I would need sponsorship. I am based in London and able to work from Stokenchurch at least three days a week. Thank you for considering my application. I would welcome the opportunity to discuss how I could contribute to CPM's AI work.",
